Assembler Version 04
====================
Assembled by: Version 03

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
This is the first two-pass assembler in the bootstrap chain, enabling forward
references. It also adds relative branch label resolution and significantly
expands the instruction table. Two-pass assembly is a major architectural
change: pass 1 collects all label definitions, pass 2 resolves references
and emits code.

Instruction mnemonics (significantly expanded):
  ADC# ADCZ AND# ASLA BCC BCS BEQ BITZ BMI BNE BPL BRK CLC CMP# CMP,Y
  EORZ INCZ INX INY JMP JSR LDA# LDAZ(),Y LDA,X LDA,Y LDAZ LDAZ,X LDX#
  LDY# LSRA ORAZ PHA PLA RTS SBC# SBCZ SEC STA STAZ(),Y STA,X STA,Y STAZ
  STAZ,X TAY TYA

  New instructions: AND#, EORZ, LDAZ(),Y (was LDA(),Y), LDA,X, LDAZ,X,
    LSRA, PHA, PLA, STA,X, STA,Y, STAZ(),Y (was STA(),Y), TAY
  Removed: CMPZ,X, DEY

DATA directive:
  DATA $XX ...        - emit hex bytes
  DATA "string"       - emit ASCII string with \n and \\ escapes
  DATA $XXXX          - emit 16-bit value (little-endian)
  Mixed: DATA $XX "string" $XXXX on same line

Operand types in instruction arguments:
  $XX                 - 8-bit hex value
  $XXXX               - 16-bit hex value (little-endian)
  "string"            - ASCII string with \n, \\, and \" escapes
  label               - 16-bit label reference (little-endian)
  <label              - low byte of label value (1 byte emitted)
  >label              - high byte of label value (1 byte emitted)
  ~label              - relative branch offset (target - PC - 1)

Label features:
  - Labels at column 0 bound to program counter
  - label = $XXXX     - constant assignment (hex value only)
  - * = $XXXX         - set program counter (origin directive)
  - Linear search through label table at $3000
  - Forward references SUPPORTED (two-pass assembly)
  - Duplicate label detection (pass 1 only)

Two-pass assembly:
  - Pass 1 ($PASS=$00): Collects label definitions, tracks PC but does not
    emit output. Label references emit dummy bytes to maintain correct PC.
  - Pass 2 ($PASS=$FF): Resolves all label references and emits final output.
  - The emit function checks PASS and only writes to output on pass 2.
  - capturelabel only stores labels on pass 1; skips to end of line on pass 2.

Error handling:
  - Error 01: Label not found
  - Error 02: Duplicate label
  - Error 03: Opcode not found
  - Error 04: Expected hex value

Semicolon comments (to end of line).

New in this version (relative to version 03):
- Two-pass assembly enabling forward references
- ~ prefix for relative branch target labels (emitlabelrel computes
  target - PC - 1 on pass 2)
- Pass-aware emit (only writes output on pass 2)
- Pass-aware label capture (only on pass 1)
- Pass-aware label resolution (returns dummy on pass 1)
- Expanded instruction table: AND#, EORZ, LDAZ(),Y, LDA,X, LDAZ,X,
  LSRA, PHA, PLA, STA,X, STA,Y, STAZ(),Y, TAY
- Removed CMPZ,X and DEY from instruction table
- Renamed LDA(),Y to LDAZ(),Y and STA(),Y to STAZ(),Y (Z prefix indicates
  zero-page pointer)
- findintab now initializes Y=0 internally (callers no longer need to
  maintain Y=0)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
The source uses features from version 03. It uses label assignments, byte
selectors, and the origin directive that version 03 introduced, plus the
same instruction set that version 03 supports.

Source features used:
  - Non-standard instruction mnemonics from version 03's table
    (including BITZ, BMI, BPL, SBCZ which were added in version 03)
  - Labels at column 0 for code locations
  - label = $XXXX constant assignments for all variables
    (TEMP, NEXTCHAR, TABL, TABH, PCL, PCH, HEX1, HEX2, PASS, TOKEN, LBTAB)
  - * = $2000 origin directive
  - <label byte selectors for zero-page operands
  - >label byte selectors for high-byte extraction
  - Label references as 16-bit operands
  - DATA directive with hex bytes and string literals
  - Character string operands in instructions (e.g., CMP# "\n")
  - Hex operands ($XX, $XXXX)
  - Semicolon comments
  - Branch targets as hardcoded hex offsets (not yet using ~ for branches)

New syntax used in source (relative to version 03):
- * = $2000 origin directive
- label = $XXXX constant assignments for zero-page variables

Other source changes:
- BRK with inline data on single line (BRK $01 "Label not found" $00)
  instead of separate BRK and DATA lines
- PASS variable and BITZ/BMI/BPL used for two-pass control flow
